From 95d93d35109d478fe803b32da68ad8ac9487d120 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Drive Player <drive-player@localhost>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 03:47:20 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] h26x: time only the start of the stream for the packetizer

The demuxer gave each block it read the time of the start, and the H.264
packetizer takes the time of a block that begins a picture as that
picture's decoding time, setting its clock to it. The presentation times
it derives from the order of the pictures went on, so the offset between
the two grew at each block, and the demuxer, which keeps that offset,
put the pictures later and later: a stream whose pictures are small, many
to a block, was shown at half its rate and then jumped. Only the first
block after the start is now timed, and the packetizer times the
pictures after it at their rate.
---
 modules/demux/mpeg/h26x.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/modules/demux/mpeg/h26x.c b/modules/demux/mpeg/h26x.c
index 44d8e08..23074c7 100644
--- a/modules/demux/mpeg/h26x.c
+++ b/modules/demux/mpeg/h26x.c
@@ -429,6 +429,13 @@ static int Demux( demux_t *p_demux)
     else
     {
         p_block_in->i_dts = date_Get( &p_sys->feed_dts );
+        /* Only the start is timed for the packetizer, which times the
+         * pictures after it at their rate and in their order. Timed again
+         * with each block, its clock went back to the start whenever a
+         * picture began a block, while the order of the pictures moved
+         * their presentation on: pictures many to a block were shown late
+         * and then skipped. */
+        date_Set( &p_sys->feed_dts, VLC_TICK_INVALID );
     }
 
     while( (p_block_out = p_sys->p_packetizer->pf_packetize( p_sys->p_packetizer,
